-- equality cases (must be ~ratio 1; lower bound may land just under)
t=0 (W[h_K] = K)                             t=0.00 LHS=4.000000 volW in [3.995713, 4.000000]  ratio_lb=0.998928  NEAR-EQUALITY (outer >= LHS, bound too loose)
dilates K, 3K (W = 3^t K)                    t=0.50 LHS=7.794229 volW in [7.788558, 7.794648]  ratio_lb=0.999273  NEAR-EQUALITY (outer >= LHS, bound too loose)
-- note: boxes with COMMON axes are an equality case: Hoelder gives box(a^(1-t)b^t) inside W and
   the axis constraints give W inside that box, so W = box(a^(1-t) b^t) exactly (ratio 1).
